{"acceptance_length": 5.869565217391305, "acceptance_lengths": [9, 8, 1, 2, 2, 8, 2, 2, 3, 3, 9, 11, 6, 9, 11, 10, 9, 2, 1, 9, 3, 3, 5, 12, 10, 3, 8, 8, 9, 4, 2, 3, 3, 1, 4, 3, 1, 11, 4, 2, 8, 13, 5, 12, 9, 7], "accepted_draft_lengths": [8, 7, 0, 1, 1, 7, 1, 1, 2, 2, 8, 10, 5, 8, 10, 9, 8, 1, 0, 8, 2, 2, 4, 11, 9, 2, 7, 7, 8, 3, 1, 2, 2, 0, 3, 2, 0, 10, 3, 1, 7, 12, 4, 11, 8, 6], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "Let's break this down step by step.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Calculate the cost of bus trips per week**\n\nJanet takes **2 bus trips per day**, and she does this **5 days a week**.\n\nSo, the total number of bus trips per week is:\n\n$$\n2 \\text{ trips/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days/week} = 10 \\text{ trips/week}\n$$\n\nEach trip costs **$2.20**, so the total cost per week for bus trips is:\n\n$$\n10 \\text{ trips} \\times \\$2.20/\\text{trip} = \\$22.00\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Compare with the cost of a weekly bus pass**\n\nA weekly bus pass costs **$20**.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Calculate the savings**\n\nTo find how much Janet would save by buying the weekly bus pass instead of paying for individual trips:\n\n$$\n\\text{Savings} = \\text{Cost of trips} - \\text{Cost of pass} = \\$22.00 - \\$20.00 = \\$2.00\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 **Final Answer:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\$2.00}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 1.6743011260405183, "draft_calls": 46, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 66, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "ece1269540becf19b73b75b0ca48a5dfd6178ffe372c6606870efbbab8ae580a", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "363fda6ecd2b7559a873f50fa0168d55fae7ca56b6dd9e847cb04afa078cc515", "output_tokens": 271, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23425642496, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23741857792, "problem_id": "gsm8k/1084abb10503718a", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 288.27692794799805, "prefill_full_target": 31.865087509155273, "prefill_relay": 0.3089599907398224, "relay"