{"acceptance_length": 5.971830985915493, "acceptance_lengths": [4, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 12, 6, 2, 5, 1, 16, 2, 8, 2, 1, 13, 2, 16, 9, 5, 16, 4, 3, 3, 8, 1, 12, 16, 16, 13, 2, 4, 1, 9, 7, 1, 4, 1, 3, 2, 4, 6, 14, 9, 11, 6, 5, 1, 5, 5, 4, 4, 2, 2, 5, 4, 3, 6, 2, 3, 4, 11, 11, 13, 16, 16, 3, 7, 4], "accepted_draft_lengths": [3, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 11, 5, 1, 4, 0, 15, 1, 7, 1, 0, 12, 1, 15, 8, 4, 15, 3, 2, 2, 7, 0, 11, 15, 15, 12, 1, 3, 0, 8, 6, 0, 3, 0, 2, 1, 3, 5, 13, 8, 10, 5, 4, 0, 4, 4, 3, 3, 1, 1, 4, 3, 2, 5, 1, 2, 3, 10, 10, 12, 15, 15, 2, 6, 3], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23321325568, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23321308160, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given a word problem that involves some arithmetic and algebra. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the first part of the problem\n\n> **\"Gomer ate 5 less than 23 scoops of mashed potatoes.\"**\n\nThis means:\n\n$$\n\\text{Scoops Gomer ate} = 23 - 5 = 18 \\text{ scoops}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Understand the second part of the problem\n\n> **\"It takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes.\"**\n\nLet's parse this carefully.\n\n- \"3 less than 6 potatoes\" means:\n  $$\n  6 - 3 = 3 \\text{ potatoes}\n  $$\n\n- \"1 less than 3 scoops\" means:\n  $$\n  3 - 1 = 2 \\text{ scoops}\n  $$\n\nSo, the statement is saying:\n\n> **\"It takes 3 potatoes to make 2 scoops of mashed potatoes.\"**\n\nThis gives us a **rate** of potatoes per scoop:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3 \\text{ potatoes}}{2 \\text{ scoops}} = \\frac{3}{2} \\text{ potatoes per scoop}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Use the rate to find how many potatoes Gomer ate\n\nWe know Gomer ate **18 scoops** of mashed potatoes.\n\nUsing the rate of **3 potatoes per 2 scoops**, we can find the number of potatoes:\n\n$$\n\\text{Potatoes eaten} = 18 \\text{ scoops} \\times \\frac{3 \\text{ potatoes}}{2 \\text{ scoops}} = \\frac{18 \\times 3}{2} = \\frac{54}{2} = 27\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{27}\n$$\n\nGomer ate **27 potatoes**.", "decode_seconds": 2.597297940403223, "draft_calls": 71, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 76, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "16cf8c2000e8b55e51ce3c60c7707d0a98229e4818cf9471a234fa20e7bc660b", "method": "relay_svd1536", "output_hash": "de94aa88bc4957ac38c50c65eaf403d451aee068b06f3240fb3c30fb29d0f957", "output_tokens": 423, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23459446272, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23750246400, "problem_id": "gsm8k/15e53aebc2660282", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 445.93596935272217, "prefill_full_target": 32.34329605102539, "prefill_relay": 0.16140800714492798, "relay": 15.282975971698761, "unattributed_runtime": 29.279245037585497, "verification_full_target": 2108.7068195343018}, "proposal_lengths": [15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15], "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "27", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 2.6317097139544785, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 23750246400, "reserved_memory_before_bytes": 23750246400, "target_calls": 71, "time_to_first_token_seconds": 0.0325590749271214, "turn_index": 0}
